WEBVTT

00:00:00.838 --> 00:00:02.246
Welcome to vNAAATS.

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:06.438
This is a quick how-to on installing the vNAAATS plugin in EuroScope.

00:00:07.558 --> 00:00:11.174
once you have downloaded the latest version of the vNAAATS package.

00:00:11.398 --> 00:00:14.278
obtained your key from the Gander Oceanic website.

00:00:14.566 --> 00:00:17.926
and added these to your vnaaats.cfg file.

00:00:18.182 --> 00:00:20.070
It is time to set up EuroScope.

00:00:20.998 --> 00:00:25.190
First, select the OC of vNAAATS profile to open EuroScope.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.238
Click Open SCT. Choose Load Sector File.

00:00:31.494 --> 00:00:35.014
and select the latest EXCXO NAT sector file.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.374
Ensure the vNAAATS plugin is loaded in the plugin dialog box.

00:00:51.046 --> 00:00:54.374
Then click Open SCT and New vNAAATS display.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.422
The blue menu bar should appear.

00:00:57.542 --> 00:01:04.358
Lastly, once again, click Open SCT, then Open, and navigate to your EXCXO folder.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.062
Find the ASR folder and click on the vNAAATS.asr file.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:10.982
You're now ready to control.

00:01:11.302 --> 00:01:14.662
We suggest you save this profile when exiting your EuroScope.

